id: pm-web-ccie
title: Offline mutation queue is not bound to the originating account or idempotency key
description: "Offline API mutations are stored with method, path, and body but no authenticated user identity or idempotency key. If a browser changes accounts before reconnecting, replay uses the current session; if a response is lost after the server commits, retry can repeat a non-idempotent mutation. The CSRF work in pm-web-413z deliberately repairs token freshness without pretending to solve account ownership or exactly-once delivery."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: idempotency,multi-user,offline,security
created_at: "2026-08-30T21:39:59.317Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T20:40:02.315Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Every queued mutation is durably bound to the authenticated user/session that created it; a different account never replays it; unknown legacy ownership is preserved and surfaced for explicit recovery without blocking unrelated owned records; every mutation carries a server-enforced idempotency key so retry after an ambiguous response cannot duplicate state; real browser/service-worker/PostgreSQL tests cover logout/login, account switching, lost responses, restart, queue ordering, and zero data loss."
why_now: The CSRF review proved queue records survive browser sessions and surfaced the adjacent cross-account and ambiguous-retry risks; multi-user production readiness requires explicit ownership and exactly-once semantics.
reviewer: security-review
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-web 2026.8.29 offline service-worker queue
repro_steps: "Queue a mutation while authenticated as user A, change the browser session to user B before reconnecting, then flush; the request is authenticated as B. Separately, let the server commit a non-idempotent mutation but drop the response; the retained record retries without an idempotency key."
expected_result: Queued work remains owned by its creator and ambiguous retries are exactly-once.
actual_result: Replay uses whichever session is current and has no deduplication identity.
affected_version: 2026.8.29
component: Offline mutation queue
customer_impact: "A shared browser can attribute pending work to the wrong user, and a network ambiguity can duplicate mutations."
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T18:15:59.802Z",claude-orchestrator,"PR #170: queued mutations are stamped with the broadcast account (persisted session store), target workspace and an idempotency key generated before the first network attempt; foreign, unknown-owner and logged-out records are never replayed or deleted, and surface MUTATIONS_BLOCKED with a visible explicit recovery action that adopts unknown-owner records for the current account (assigning a key first). Server: pm_idempotency_keys claims (account, key) atomically, replays stored outcomes, rejects a key reused for a different request (422), never stores transient 425/429 refusals, answers 409 outcome-unknown instead of re-executing a stale pending key, catches outcome-persist failures, indexes created_at and throttles the retention sweep. Implemented by the pi (GLM-5.3) and codex (gpt-6.1-sol) agents; review round 1 (12 Greptile + CodeQL findings) fixed test-first. Local release:check: 451/451 tests pass."
  "2026-10-04T18:29:41.302Z",codex-sol,"Read all seven PR #170 round-two findings. Plan: failing worker interleaving tests and real HTTP/PostgreSQL guard regressions, then bind request identity before sending, verify expected accounts on the server, serialize adoption and flush, exclude auth routes, and run retention before claims. Full release gates and explicit-path commit/push follow verification."
  "2026-10-04T18:39:28.448Z",codex-sol,"Test-first receipt: focused real-PostgreSQL/HTTP and worker suites reported 55 tests, 44 pass, 11 fail before production fixes. The failures reproduced all seven findings, including two-account first-attempt, replay, recovery and overlapping-adoption interleavings. Added expected-account refusal before key claims, captured owner before sending, serialized recovery and flush, transactional adoption preserving keys, auth exclusions, existing-user checks, and pre-claim retention."
  "2026-10-04T18:48:46.525Z",codex-sol,"Focused suites passed 57/57. Lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates passed. The first full release run used the implicit sibling directory as its fleet root and saw unrelated worktrees, causing three catalog/snapshot assertions to fail (459/462 pass). The supported PM_FLEET_ROOT override points at the canonical fleet; all 12 catalog assertions pass with that setting. Retry the full release gate with this repo-relative environment override. Hardened cleanup-failure injection with a connection-scoped PostgreSQL statement trigger to avoid dependence on concurrent retention sweeps."
  "2026-10-04T18:53:44.872Z",codex-sol,"PR #170 round two: all seven findings fixed. 4178787252: capture the tab account before sending and preserve it after network failure. 4178787257: every replay sends X-PM-Expected-Account; the server returns 409 before execution or key claiming on mismatch, keeping the record. 4178739144: REBIND_RECORDS carries the approving account and the server verifies recovery approval. 4178739147: adoption and flush serialize; adoption reads and writes in one IndexedDB transaction and keeps existing keys. 4178739152: auth routes never queue, key or replay stored responses, including legacy auth records. 4178787261: missing/deleted token users bypass keying; live login/logout work. 4178787264: retention runs before claims; a real PostgreSQL cleanup failure leaves no pending key and retry succeeds. Test-first reproduction: 55 tests, 44 pass, 11 fail; focused fixed suites: 57/57. Final npm run release:check passed through pm test with PM_FLEET_ROOT=../../fleet: 462/462 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 33 source files reported; coverage 85.00% lines, 81.45% branches, 78.61% functions; thresholds unchanged at 79/79/75. Lint/typecheck/build, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, packed npm/Bun acceptance, changelog and release verification passed. Whole-repository four-metric 100% coverage remains outside this review slice. README and test links updated; leave the item open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-04T20:06:36.437Z",codex-sol,"Review round 3: read comments 4179117062 and 4179117055 in full. Add failing real PostgreSQL/HTTP and worker recovery tests first. Release only provably pre-commit claims; settle ambiguous outcomes explicitly, preserve workspace ordering, add confirmed retry-as-new/discard and persistent notice dismissal. Run full release gate before committing and pushing."
  "2026-10-04T20:14:53.076Z",codex-sol,"Red tests reproduced three server failures (missing in-flight/unknown codes and same-key retry stuck after real rollback), two worker recovery/order failures, and two SPA recovery/dismiss failures. Implementing durable pending/completed/outcome_unknown states with settlement-based retention. A confirmed pre-COMMIT rollback releases the key; a COMMIT attempt remains ambiguous even if ROLLBACK later succeeds. FIFO applies per owned workspace, with account-level writes acting as cross-workspace barriers. Attention records require confirmed fresh-key retry or discard."
  "2026-10-04T20:22:59.067Z",codex-sol,"The first full release run exposed a test-environment mismatch: catalog checks treated sibling worktrees as the fleet. The documented PM_FLEET_ROOT override, set to ../../fleet, passes all 12 catalog checks against the actual fleet. Keep the catalog and committed snapshot unchanged; use this override for the full gate. Quota forecast remains within its weekly limit."
  "2026-10-04T20:28:39.111Z",codex-sol,"PR #170 round three: 4179117062 fixed with explicit pending/completed/outcome_unknown PostgreSQL states, machine-readable 409 codes, handler-proven pre-commit claim release, stale-intent settlement, and retention from settlement. Worker unknown outcomes and three consecutive 5xx failures persist needs-attention; owned workspace FIFO and account-level barriers preserve ordering while other workspaces flush. Recovery offers owner-verified, user-confirmed Retry as a new request with a fresh key, and Discard. 4179117055 fixed with an aria-labelled native Dismiss button and suppression until the blocked set changes. Red regressions were observed before fixes. Final tracker-linked npm run release:check passed with PM_FLEET_ROOT=../../fleet: 469 tests, 469 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 33 source files reported; 85.02% lines, 81.47% branches, 78.58% functions; thresholds unchanged at 79/79/75. Typecheck/build/lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, packed npm/Bun acceptance, changelog and release verification passed. Test coverage includes real pre-commit rollback with same-key success, ambiguous commit without automatic re-execution, approved new-key execution once, other-workspace progress, same-workspace FIFO/account-level barriers, discard, confirmation cancellation, and dismissal persistence. Open limits: approved new requests can duplicate an unknown original commit; deduplication expires after the configured retention window; whole-repository four-metric 100% coverage is not established. Leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-04T20:40:02.315Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeQL on PR #170 flagged the workspace-recovery test harness (cookie middleware without CSRF, handlers without rate limiting). The harness now mounts the production csrfProtection and write-tier limiter before the idempotency guard, matching the hosted middleware order; all 9 HTTP recovery tests pass through them."
